    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/636865b8cca0a0a962c21f3f/n1PEv1RXr_QrhK7DIZbOg.png) ⟨28⟩\nAI4Manufacturing⟨28⟩\n/\nD14-editbench-annotated⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] AI4Manufacturing 13\nModalities:  Text ⟨31⟩\nFormats:  parquet ⟨32⟩\nSize:  < 1K ⟨33⟩\nArXiv:\narxiv: 2605.10865\nTags:  smart-manufacturing ⟨34⟩ sft ⟨35⟩ industrial ⟨36⟩ vision ⟨37⟩ cad ⟨38⟩ cadquery ⟨39⟩ + 2\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨40⟩ pandas ⟨41⟩ Polars ⟨42⟩ + 1\nLicense:\nother\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨43⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨44⟩ Community ⟨45⟩\n##  You need to agree to share your contact information to access this dataset\nThis repository is publicly accessible, but you have to accept the conditions to access its files and content.\nThis dataset is released for **research use**. Please state your name, affiliation, and intended use.\nLog in⟨46⟩ or Sign Up⟨47⟩ to review the conditions and access this dataset content.\n  * Pipeline (improve-never-drop)⟨48⟩\n  * Schema⟨49⟩\n  * Roles⟨50⟩\n  * Provenance & caveats⟨51⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨52⟩ D14 EditBench Annotated — CAD code editing with chain-of-thought \nThe **`edit_bench`layer of D14 (BenchCAD)** with teacher-written reasoning: **748 records** , each `CadQuery program + edit instruction → reasoning → edited program`. The `reasoning` ends with the complete program in a ```python block, and the program is **AST-equivalent to BenchCAD's execution-verified reference — asserted per record at assembly** (records whose regeneration drifted carry the reference spliced verbatim; correctness is never sampled).\nSibling releases: `AI4Manufacturing/D14-codegen-annotated`⟨53⟩ (the other trainable D14 layer) and `AI4Manufacturing/D14-vision-qa`⟨54⟩ (the Vision-QA layer — an evaluation probe, deliberately NOT training data).\n##   ⟨48⟩ Pipeline (improve-never-drop) \n  1. **Generation** (Claude Sonnet 5, batched): gold-shown reasoning + code regeneration; hard no-leak prompt (the reasoning never references the provided program).\n  2. **Deterministic checks** : AST code-equivalence, leakage regex, truncation.\n  3. **Faithfulness screen** (Claude Sonnet 5 as grounded judge: sees the render + reference + reasoning): flags prose that misdescribes the part or narrates a construction different from the actual program.\n  4. **Regeneration** of flagged records with the judge's critique; re-screened; kept only if clean. Stubborn records fall back to best-prose + pasted-gold code. **No record is dropped** ; every verdict is preserved in `metadata.cot`.\n\n\n**Prose faithfulness: 86% of records score ≥3** (judge scale 1–5). The residual ~14% carry guaranteed-correct code with their (flagged) prose verdict documented in `metadata.cot` — filterable via `metadata.cot.screen.faithfulness` / `metadata.cot.method`.\n##   ⟨49⟩ Schema \nUnchanged from the source (`query`, `image`, `annot`, `cate`, `task`, `other_files`) except: `reasoning` filled (prose + ```python program); `metadata` gains a `cot` provenance block (`annotator_model`, `method` = rationalized / rationalized_regenerated / rationalized_pasted / +code_pasted variants, `code_equivalent` (always true), screen + final judge verdicts). Reasoning prose may use light markdown structure (headers/bold), typical of code-reasoning corpora.\n##   ⟨50⟩ Roles \n**Roles:** `reasoning` is the SFT imitation target — its terminal ````python` block is the model-facing deliverable; `annot` is the machine-parseable gold used for verification and reward parsing, **not** an output-format target.\nNote: the gold key inside `annot` is `gt_code` here (its codegen sibling uses `code`).\n##   ⟨51⟩ Provenance & caveats \n  * Derived from `AI4Manufacturing/benchcad_TB3E1_D14`⟨55⟩ (= **BenchCAD** , arXiv:2605.10865). Please cite BenchCAD.\n  * `reasoning` is **teacher-generated and model-gated** , not human-verified; the reference programs are BenchCAD's execution-verified golds and are never altered.\n  * BenchCAD is published as an evaluation benchmark; if you also evaluate on BenchCAD, note that training on this dataset contaminates that comparison.\n\n\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    42\nTotal file size: 110 MB\n##  Paper for AI4Manufacturing/D14-editbench-annotated\n#### BenchCAD: A Comprehensive, Industry-Standard Benchmark for Programmatic CAD Paper • 2605.10865 • Published May 12 • 1 ⟨56⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨57⟩ Privacy⟨58⟩ About⟨59⟩ Careers⟨60⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
